WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.610
Fans of the Marvel Cinematic Universe got
an early Christmas present when it was announced

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.959
in December 2017 that Disney would be acquiring
a large portion of Fox - including the movie

00:00:09.959 --> 00:00:13.019
rights to the X-Men and the Fantastic Four.

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:17.849
With the dream of the a unified MCU finally
on the verge of becoming reality, here's a

00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:21.880
look at all the best Marvel characters Disney
is getting from Fox.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.179
Wolverine and The X-Men

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:29.089
Obviously, the biggest question for fans is
what Marvel will do with Fox's massive X-Men

00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:34.460
franchise, which has so far produced three
solo Wolverine films as well as six X-Men

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.710
movies, with a seventh on the way in 2018.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:42.010
Merging the X-Men franchise with the MCU would
be a massive undertaking.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.410
Should they recast the roles and reboot the
X-men entirely?

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:50.280
Or should they use the X-Men franchise's frequent
timeline shifts and retcons to simply add

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.280
the whole existing X-men universe to the MCU?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.719
If you thought understanding the X-Men films
was difficult before, get ready for a wild

00:00:57.719 --> 00:00:58.719
ride.

00:00:58.719 --> 00:00:59.719
Will Wolverine make the leap?

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:04.830
"I go where I wanna go."

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.500
The Fantastic Four

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.540
Even though they've appeared in four movies
to date, the Fantastic Four have never truly

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.860
"worked" onscreen.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.340
So for fans, the most exciting thing about
the Disney-Fox merger is the possibility that

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.340
we'll finally get a good Fantastic Four movie.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.660
So far, they've been, well…

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.750
"Two guys, a girl, and a thing nobody wanted."

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:29.400
At their heart, the Fantastic Four aren't
superheroes, they're adventurers, using science

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.020
and superpowers to explore other dimensions,
other realities, and the unknown depths of

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.240
our universe.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.670
Films like Thor, The Guardians of the Galaxy,
and Doctor Strange have introduced some of

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:44.990
the weirder corners of the MCU to fans - but
it's the Fantastic Four who are best designed

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:46.140
to explore them.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.140
We can't wait!

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.140
Galactus

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.100
"I am Galactus!

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.761
The be all and end all of the universe!"

00:01:57.761 --> 00:02:02.080
The biggest and baddest villain in the Marvel
universe, Galactus literally eats planets

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.250
for breakfast.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.720
So fans were terribly disappointed when Fox
wasted him in Fantastic Four: Rise of the

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.769
Silver Surfer by showing him as just an angry
space cloud instead of the world-devouring

00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:14.510
giant from the comics.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:19.709
Of course, Galactus never goes anywhere alone,
and his coming to Disney also means that Marvel

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:25.109
Studios has the rights to all his heralds—not
just the Silver Surfer, but others including

00:02:25.109 --> 00:02:31.550
the loyal Air-Walker, the villainous Morg,
the adventurous Nova, and the ambitious Terrax.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:35.260
Once Thanos is through as a threat, don't
be surprised if you start hearing rumblings

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:40.310
of Galactus as the next big bad worthy of
a franchise-spanning team-up.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.780
Silver Surfer

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.609
Speaking of the sentinel of the spaceways,
the Silver Surfer didn't exactly blow people

00:02:46.609 --> 00:02:49.829
away when he made his big screen debut in
2006.

00:02:49.829 --> 00:02:55.120
But his tragic story of sacrifice and loss,
where he gives up his freedom to save humanity,

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.530
is timeless.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.219
Add in his iconic design, and you have a character
with the potential to become a breakout star

00:03:01.219 --> 00:03:03.459
in the MCU.

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:04.459
Deadpool

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:09.780
Fans have to be salivating at the idea of
Deadpool joining the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:14.360
Some of the funniest jokes in the surprise
2016 smash hit film involved Ryan Reynolds

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.329
playing off of the strait laced X-Men.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.329
"It's a big house.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:18.730
It's funny that I only ever see two of you.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:22.280
It's like the studio couldn't afford another
x-man."

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:26.550
Now imagine what he'll be able to do when
he gets to run into characters like Dr. Strange,

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.709
Tony Stark, or even Spider-Man?

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:31.819
We can't wait to hear the one-liners fly.

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:32.819
Legion

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:38.250
It's safe to say that nobody outside of hardcore
comic book fans had ever heard of the character

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:43.889
Legion until FX debuted the critically acclaimed
TV series starring Downton Abbey's Dan Stevens.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:48.569
Now, though, the character provides some intriguing
possibilities thanks to his connection to

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:52.260
the X-Men universe through deadbeat dad Professor
Xavier.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:56.810
And his reality-warping powers could be a
handy way to easily write him into any franchise

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.840
the honchos at Marvel Studios want.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.540
The possibilities are endless - and intriguing.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.279
The New Mutants

00:04:04.279 --> 00:04:08.770
The next generation of students at Charles
Xavier's school for gifted cannon fodder,

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:14.230
the New Mutants are finally coming to the
big screen in 2018 with a horror tinged adaptation

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.570
of the classic Demon Bear storyline.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:21.700
While the film only focuses on a handful of
characters, including Magik, Wolfsbane, Cannonball,

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:27.250
Sunspot, and Mirage, the New Mutants lineup
also includes a number of other fan favorites,

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:29.620
like Karma, Warlock, and Magma.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.890
Traditionally aimed at a slightly younger
demographic than X-Men, it will be interesting

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:39.470
to see how - or if - the New Mutants fit into
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.170
Alpha Flight

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:47.370
In February 2017, X-Men producer Simon Kinberg
made reference to an in-the-works "X-Flight"

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:52.280
movie, which many took to be referring to
a new version of the never-before-adapted

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.140
team Alpha Flight.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:58.510
Formed by the Canadian government with the
help of Wolverine, Alpha Flight has strong

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:03.310
ties to the X-Men universe while still maintaining
its own identity thanks to unique and offbeat

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:08.440
characters like Shaman, Puck, Northstar, Snowbird,
and Sasquatch.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:12.560
In a world where the Guardians of the Galaxy
have become household names, with a little

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:17.670
tender loving care from Marvel Studios, Alpha
Flight could become the next big thing.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.620
Dr. Doom

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:23.780
One of the most awesome developments from
the Disney-Fox deal doesn't involve the heroes

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:29.550
it brings into the MCU, but rather the villains—and
no Marvel Comics villain is more thoroughly

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.870
iconic than Doctor Doom.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:36.430
While Doom is mostly known for his eternal
rivalry with the Fantastic Four, the ruler

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:41.360
of Latveria has also gone toe-to-toe with
just about everyone else in the MCU.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.690
So far, fans haven't been thrilled with the
way he's been portrayed in the Fox movies,

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:50.710
so a Doom that actually lives up to the character's
great legacy in the comics would be a very

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:51.970
welcome change.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.540
And if you think otherwise…

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.040
"You're wrong!"

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.660
Kang the Conqueror

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:05.130
He's considered to be the Avengers' ultimate
archenemy, battling Earth's Mightiest Heroes

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.260
dozens of times over the decades.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:11.530
But thanks to a quirk in their licensing deal,
the movie rights for Kang were apparently

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:16.550
shipped over to Fox along with the Fantastic
Four, meaning the Avengers were left without

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:17.740
their greatest foe.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:22.930
Now, though, it's possible that the time traveling
warlord Kang, who has conquered countless

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:28.730
empires throughout history, will finally get
to set his sights on the 21st century MCU.

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:31.180
All we can say is, it's about time!

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.230
Thanks for watching!

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:35.050
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:37.270
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

